# LLM, RAG, and agent products

Loads when prompt, eval, RAG, or vendor-SDK files are in play. Harness, tools, sandbox, trajectory evals, coding-agent SDLC: `agentic-development.md`.

## Prompts and models

- Treat prompts, tools, and model IDs as versioned interfaces. A prompt change without an eval is an untested API change.
- Pin model slugs. Do not use floating `:latest`. Record provider, model, temperature, and max tokens in traces.
- Prefer structured outputs (JSON schema / tool calls) over free text when downstream code parses the result.
- System prompts must state refusal policy, tool limits, and what the model is not allowed to invent.

## RAG

- Chunking, embedding model, and index ID are config. Re-embed when the embedding model changes; never mix vectors from two models in one index.
- Retrieval must be measurable: recall@k on a labeled set, empty-retrieval behavior, and citation of sources in the answer when the product claims grounding.
- If retrieval returns nothing, refuse or say so. Do not let the model answer from parametric memory when the product is “answer from docs.”
- Metadata filters (tenant, ACL, locale) apply before similarity search. Vector search is not an authorization layer.

## Agents and tools

- Tool allowlists. No unconstrained shell, SQL, or HTTP from a model in production. Each tool has a schema, timeout, and audit log.
- Bound the loop: max steps, max tokens, wall-clock. Detect and stop cycles. Idempotent tools with an idempotency key from the workflow.
- Human-in-the-loop for irreversible actions (email send, payment, delete, production deploy) unless the product explicitly automates that action with a signed policy.

## Evals

- Golden sets live in the repo or an eval store, not in chat history. Run them on prompt and model changes.
- Track groundedness, task success, latency, cost, and safety (PII, jailbreak, harmful assistance) as first-class scores.
- Shadow or A/B before replacing a production prompt. Keep the previous prompt version deployable.

## Cost, privacy, reliability

- Budget tokens per request and per session. Cache stable prefixes. Fail closed on 429s with backoff; do not infinite-retry paid APIs.
- Redact PII before third-party APIs unless the vendor is contracted and the data class is allowed. Never log raw prompts that contain secrets or customer data.
- Timeouts and circuit breakers on every model and tool call. Degrade to a safe fallback (cached answer, “try again”, human queue) — not a hallucinated success.
